## 2. Integration Points

### BottomSheetModalProvider Placement
The `BottomSheetModalProvider` will be wrapped around the tab navigator in `app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` to ensure it's available across all tabs while maintaining proper z-index ordering:

```tsx
// app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx
import { BottomSheetModalProvider } from '@gorhom/bottom-sheet';

export default function TabsLayout() {
  return (
    <BottomSheetModalProvider>
      {/* Tab navigator content */}
    </BottomSheetModalProvider>
  );
}
```

### Home-to-Sheet Data Flow
1. Home screen concert cards receive `onPress` handlers
2. On press, Home sets state for selected concert and opens sheet
3. Sheet receives concert data via props and manages its own presentation state

```tsx
// In Home component
const [selectedEvent, setSelectedEvent] = useState<EventWithArtist | null>(null);
const [sheetVisible, setSheetVisible] = useState(false);

// Press handler
const handleEventPress = (event: EventWithArtist) => {
  setSelectedEvent(event);
  setSheetVisible(true);
};

// Render
{selectedEvent && sheetVisible && (
  <ConcertDetailSheet 
    event={selectedEvent} 
    onDismiss={() => {
      setSelectedEvent(null);
      setSheetVisible(false);
    }}
  />
)}
```

### Presentation/Dismissal Mechanism
- Imperative control via state (`sheetVisible` and `selectedEvent`)
- Backdrop touch and downward swipe dismiss via BottomSheetModal's `onClose`
- Header back button provides explicit dismiss action

