## 6. Edge Cases

### Missing Image Handling
```tsx
<Image 
  source={{
    uri: event.artist?.image_url || 'https://via.placeholder.com/400x400?text=Sin+imagen',
  }}
  style={styles.artistPhoto}
/>
```
- Fallback to placeholder service when `image_url` is null/undefined
- Placeholder shows "Sin imagen" text on gray background

### Missing URL Handling
```tsx
<TouchableOpacity 
  style={[styles.actionButton, !event.url && styles.disabledButton]}
  disabled={!event.url}
  onPress={event.url ? handleUrlPress : undefined}
>
  <Text style={styles.actionButtonText}>
    {event.url ? 'Ver Entradas' : 'Sin enlace'}
  </Text>
</TouchableOpacity>
```
- Button visually dimmed when no URL available
- Press handler only attached when URL exists
- Text changes to indicate lack of link

### Legacy Events Without Source/URL
- Database migration allows NULL values for new columns
- Existing events will have `null` for `source` and `url`
- UI gracefully handles null values:
  - Source field not displayed in UI (used internally for analytics)
  - URL absence handled as described above
  - No breaking changes to existing functionality

### Platform-Specific Considerations
- **iOS**: Bottom sheet handle uses native appearance cues
- **Android**: Handle follows material design guidelines
- **Overflow menu**: Uses platform-appropriate presentation via `react-native-action-sheet`
- **Share API**: Uses `react-native-share` which handles platform differences internally

### Error Boundaries
- Network errors during delete/share operations show toast notifications
- Invalid URLs are handled by Share API/linking library
- Missing artist data falls back to "Artista desconocido" and placeholder images